# <vault>/.feed-clip-feeds: release and blog feeds the clip pipeline pulls.
#
# One feed per line:   <feed-url> [label]
# `#` starts a comment. The label prefixes the clip title ("Claude Code: v2.1.0").
# RSS, Atom and GitHub releases.atom feeds work. Each run clips at most 3 new
# entries per feed, newest first; the rest arrive on later runs. A feed that
# fails is reported on one line and never fails the run.
# Login-walled hosts (x.com, instagram.com, reddit.com) are refused.
#
# Run:  node <obsidian-triage plugin dir>/tools/feed-clip.mjs --vault <this vault> --dry-run
# prints what it would clip and writes nothing. Entries already clipped are
# remembered in .feed-clip-seen.jsonl.
#
# The codex and t3code release feeds include pre-release and nightly builds.
# Anthropic's engineering blog publishes no feed; add it here when it does.

